From: morse-backport <local@morse-backport>
Subject: dts: rp1: Enable rp1_dma so dw-spi can use DMA

The RP1 SPI controllers (snps,dw-apb-ssi) reference &rp1_dma in their
dmas property, but the rp1_dma node ships with status="disabled" in
upstream rp1.dtsi. This forces dw-spi into PIO mode for all RP1 SPI
transfers, which has FIFO/timing issues with chained SDIO-over-SPI
half-duplex transactions (e.g. Morse Micro MM6108 cmd53 reads).

Set rp1_dma status="okay". The DW_AXI_DMAC driver (CONFIG_DW_AXI_DMAC=y)
matches the snps,axi-dma-1.01a compatible and binds the controller.
SPI_DW_DMA=y enables the DMA path in spi-dw-core.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/broadcom/rp1.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/broadcom/rp1.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/broadcom/rp1.dtsi
@@ -1092,7 +1092,7 @@
 			snps,block-size = <0x40000 0x40000 0x40000 0x40000 0x40000 0x40000 0x40000 0x40000>;
 			snps,priority = <0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7>;
 			snps,axi-max-burst-len = <4>;
-			status = "disabled";
+			status = "okay";
 		};

 		rp1_usb0: usb@200000 {
